    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0116_9c88fe37a7f1.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 162px;\" /><br /><br />A and B have the same alignment of the transmission axis. Let&#39;s assume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is introduced at <math><mi>&#952;</mi></math> angle,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></math>."
